  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reintroduccin de pecares en el Parque Nacional Jeannette Kawas: restaurando las presas del.jaguar y una especie paisaje</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to support the conservation of jaguars in Jeannette Kawas National Park in Honduras through a collared peccary reintroduction effort. The project is intended to conserve a critical jaguar corridor for regional connectivity by increasing the jaguar natural prey base and reducing human-jaguar conflict. Specific activities include: (1) reintroduction of a group of collared peccaries in the park; (2) community outreach to grow community support for peccary and jaguar conservation; and (3) increased SMART patrols within the park to deter illegal activities, including poaching.</narrative>
  </description>
